{
  // STRICT-NULL STAGE 4 — packages/web-host/src only.
  //
  // Same shape as stages 1-3, with one difference that matters: this one extends
  // `packages/web-host/tsconfig.json`, NOT the repo root. web-host is not in the
  // root program at all — the root `include` is `packages/desktop/src/**/*` plus
  // four named files — so extending the root would have type-checked web-host
  // under desktop's path aliases and rootDir. Extending the package's own config
  // keeps the stage measuring the thing the package actually builds.
  //
  //   bunx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.strictnull.webhost.json
  //
  // NO `types.d.ts` ENTRY, and that is deliberate rather than forgotten. Stage 2
  // shipped a config whose narrow `include` dropped `src/types.d.ts` and then
  // invented a TS7016 the real build does not have. web-host has no `.d.ts` of
  // its own (`find packages/web-host -name '*.d.ts'` is empty), so there is
  // nothing to lose here — and that was verified, not assumed: the same config
  // WITHOUT `strictNullChecks` reports 0 errors, so every error this stage shows
  // is one the flag introduced and none is an artefact of the fence.
  //
  // `include` is written out rather than inherited so the fence is readable at
  // this file; `exclude` (node_modules, dist, **/*.test.ts) comes from the
  // package config, which is also what its own build uses.
  // THE GATE, and it is the short one — this stage has NO CAP:
  //
  //   bunx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.strictnull.webhost.json 2>&1 \
  //     | grep -c "error TS"        # must print 0
  //
  // Stages 1-3 each needed a `grep -v` for errors they could not repair, plus a
  // count pin so the excluded set could not grow unnoticed. Here there is nothing
  // to exclude: `packages/web-host/src` was already clean under `strictNullChecks`
  // when this stage started. 0 in the cap, 0 outside it, because the cap is empty.
  //
  // MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED — a gate that reports 0 is worth exactly as much as the
  // proof that it looked at anything. Three checks, all repeatable:
  //   1. `--showConfig` resolves `strictNullChecks: true` and 5 files.
  //   2. The same config WITHOUT the flag also reports 0, so nothing here is an
  //      artefact of the fence (this is the check stage 2 lacked when its narrow
  //      include invented a TS7016).
  //   3. A deliberately planted `x.length` on a `string | null` parameter WAS
  //      caught (TS18047), so the flag reaches the files.
  //
  // WHAT IS OUT OF SCOPE, on purpose. The package's own config excludes
  // `**/*.test.ts`, and this stage inherits that rather than widening it — the
  // fence should measure what the package builds. Type-checking the three test
  // files as well would add two errors, only ONE of which this flag causes:
  //   static-server.unit.test.ts:411  TS2769 — appears only with the flag;
  //   backend-launcher.test.ts:90     TS2540 — a readonly assignment, present
  //                                   with and without it, so not this stage's.
  // Both are reported rather than folded in; widening the fence is its own call.
  "extends": "./packages/web-host/tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["packages/web-host/src/**/*"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strictNullChecks": true
  }
}
